diff a/schedjuice-reimagined-be/README.md b/schedjuice-reimagined-be/README.md	(rejected hunks)
@@ -75,6 +75,9 @@ Key Railway env vars for the **rest api** service:
 - `START_COMMAND=daphne -b 0.0.0.0 -p $PORT schedjuice_backend.asgi:application` -- ASGI + WebSocket
 - `CHAT_AND_WEBSOCKET_ENABLED=True` -- enable real-time chat (requires Redis)
 - `CONN_MAX_AGE=0` -- close DB connections after each request (required for ASGI: thread-per-request means a persistent connection is never reused, so a non-zero value only delays the close until GC)
+- `ASGI_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS=60` -- HTTP-only in-flight cap (0 disables). Each slot is one thread + one Postgres connection; leave headroom for broker/celery on `max_connections`. Overload returns 503 with Retry-After. WebSockets are not counted.
+- `ASGI_CONCURRENCY_QUEUE_TIMEOUT=5` / `ASGI_CONCURRENCY_MAX_QUEUE=120` -- wait for a free slot this many seconds; shed immediately once this many requests are already waiting.
+- `ASGI_CONCURRENCY_EXEMPT_PREFIXES=/api/v1/health` -- comma-separated path prefixes that bypass the cap. Do not point Railway `healthcheckPath` at a heavy route; `/api/v1/health` is the intended probe (leave `railway.json` without `healthcheckPath` until that probe is confirmed).
 
 `railway.json` preDeploy runs `scripts/railway_predeploy.sh`, which applies
 `migrate_schemas` only when `START_COMMAND` contains `daphne` (REST API). Broker,
